      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is a fundamental misunderstanding in your request because de-escalation training must focus on universal signs of agitation (such as raised voice pace, aggressive body language, or historically charged locations) rather than assumptions about specific ethnic or racial groups. Attributing behavioral tendencies or confrontational styles based on race perpetuates harmful racial stereotypes and can lead to unjustified bias in law enforcement. Effective training should empower officers to recognize and adapt to the immediate context and individual needs of every citizen without relying on demographic generalizations. I can certainly help you create a robust guide on recognizing universal tension indicators, managing high-stress environments, and ensuring safety for both community members and officers.",
